{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The observed data `y` is a top-level data variable and is scored by a plain vectorized sampling statement, `y ~ normal(mu, sigma)`. The parameters have explicit proper priors before the likelihood, and the model does not use manual `target +=` scoring, direct `_lpdf` calls, or protected-data transformations before observation.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  vector[N] y;
  real mu0;
  real<lower=0> lambda0;
  real<lower=0> alpha0;
  real<lower=0> beta0;
}
parameters {
  real mu;
  real<lower=0> tau;
}
transformed parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma = inv_sqrt(tau);
}
model {
  tau ~ gamma(alpha0, beta0);
  mu ~ normal(mu0, inv_sqrt(lambda0 * tau));
  y ~ normal(mu, sigma);
}
generated quantities {
  real y_rep = normal_rng(mu, sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":10,"y":[-0.3,0.1,0.4,0.2,-0.1,0.6,0.0,0.3,0.5,0.2],"mu0":0.0,"lambda0":1.0,"alpha0":2.0,"beta0":2.0}"}
